            {"h": "How cards move", "ul": ["On the columns you build downward in alternating colors: a red 7 goes on a black 8.", "A free cell holds one card at a time. Use it as a temporary parking space, and a card can come back out onto a column or a foundation whenever it fits.", "A foundation takes the next card of its suit: Ace first, then 2, 3 and so on.", "An empty column can take any card, or any correctly ordered run.", "Cards in a foundation can usually be left alone. Cardles can send cards up automatically when nobody needs them any more, and you can switch that off in Settings if you like to do it yourself."]},
